„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdSalute Herodion my kinsman. Greet them that be of the household of Narcissus, which are in the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqSalute Tryphena and Tryphosa, who labour in the Lord. Salute the beloved Persis, which laboured much in the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9Salute Rufus chosen in the Lord, and his mother and mine.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[Salute Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermas, Patrobas, Hermes, and the brethren which are with them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjSalute Philologus, and Julia, Nereus, and his sister, and Olympas, and all the saints which are with them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHSalute one another with an holy kiss. The churches of Christ salute you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰Now I beseech you, brethren, mark them which cause divisions and offences contrary to the doctrine which ye have learned; and avoid them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’For they that are such serve not our Lord Jesus Christ, but their own belly; and by good words and fair speeches deceive the hearts of the simple.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦For your obedience is come abroad unto all men. I am glad therefore on your behalf: but yet I would have you wise unto that which is good, and simple concerning evil.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ@And the God of peace shall bruise Satan under your feet shortly.¦layout ‚¤textÙ5The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you. Amen.¦layout©paragraphªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVTimotheus my workfellow, and Lucius, and Jason, and Sosipater, my kinsmen, salute you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:I Tertius, who wrote this epistle, salute you in the Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€Gaius mine host, and of the whole church, saluteth you. Erastus the chamberlain of the city saluteth you, and Quartus a brother.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all. Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿Now to him that is of power to stablish you according to my gospel, and the preaching of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery, which was kept secret since the world began,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«but now is made manifest, and by the scriptures of the prophets, according to the commandment of the everlasting God, made known to all nations for the obedience of faith:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ?to God only wise, be glory through Jesus Christ for ever. Amen.¦layout ‚¤textÙZWritten to the Romans from Corinthus, and sent by Phebe servant of the church at Cenchrea.¦layout¥blankªlast_verse